message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container to center the card */
body {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #f0f0f0;
}

/* Card wrapper – gives perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 800px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* Keep children in 3D space */
    cursor: pointer;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
}

/* Front side (default) */
.card::before,
.card::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    backface-visibility: hidden;      /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius: inherit;
}

.card::before {
    background: inherit;              /* Same gradient as parent */
    z-index: 1;
}

/* Back side – hidden initially */
.card::after {
    background: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* Start flipped */
    z-index: 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
    padding: 20px;
    text-align: center;
}

/* Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front content -->
        <div style="position:absolute; inset:0; display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:1.5rem; color:#fff;">
            Front Side
        </div>
        <!-- Back content (via ::after pseudo-element) -->
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a `perspective` so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | The main container that gets rotated. |
| `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each side while rotating. |
| `transition: transform .6s ease` | Smoothly animates the rotation. |
| `::before` / `::after` | Pseudo-elements used to create front/back faces. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `::after` | Starts the back face flipped. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card on hover. |

You can replace the gradient, colors, or add more content inside the card as needed. Enjoy!
